        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.54,
          "end": 235.483,
          "en": "but for the moment, that's all I need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.5,
          "end": 237.71,
          "en": "So now we have ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.71,
          "end": 240.83,
          "en": "of changing these data properties through clicks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.83,
          "end": 245.09,
          "en": "but I mentioned that I wanna dive into styling with you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.09,
          "end": 249.59,
          "en": "Well, let's say wanna highlight when a box is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.59,
          "end": 251.873,
          "en": "and we can do that with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.78,
          "end": 256.21,
          "en": "Let's say we wanna change the border color of a box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.21,
          "end": 257.27,
          "en": "if it is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.27,
          "end": 260.15,
          "en": "solve this first box, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.15,
          "end": 265.15,
          "en": "well, we can set styles either through CSS and CSS classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.06,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "or also with inline styles by using the style attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "which is a available on basically any HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 278.46,
          "en": "In there you can do things like this, border color red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.46,
          "end": 282,
          "en": "If I saved that we have a red color here on the first box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282,
          "end": 284.87,
          "en": "but of course this now always applies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.87,
          "end": 286.313,
          "en": "not just sometimes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.2,
          "end": 290.8,
          "en": "Well, we just need to bind style to a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.8,
          "end": 293.884,
          "en": "and we can do this with, v-bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.884,
          "end": 298.33,
          "en": "or the shorthand, just colon style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.33,
          "end": 302.63,
          "en": "But now here's a special thing, style and also classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 302.63,
          "end": 305.96,
          "en": "as you will see in a couple of minutes are different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.96,
          "end": 310.24,
          "en": "If you bind those dynamically with v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 310.24,
          "end": 314.65,
          "en": "you can actually use a special syntax supported by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 314.65,
          "end": 317.33,
          "en": "for these specific attributes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.33,
          "end": 319.6,
          "en": "So for a style and for a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 319.6,
          "end": 322.73,
          "en": "you can now feed in an object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 322.73,
          "end": 326.86,
          "en": "which style normally does not want, but you can use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.86,
          "end": 330.3,
          "en": "because that's a special Vue feature for styling class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330.3,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "and in there you can have your CSS property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 338.6,
          "en": "border color, however, either wrap between single quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 339.4,
          "end": 343.03,
          "en": "because we have a JavaScript object here and property names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 343.03,
          "end": 345.03,
          "en": "with dashes are not allowed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 345.03,
          "end": 349.33,
          "en": "So we either need quotes or recommended and better use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 349.33,
          "end": 353.64,
          "en": "the camel case version of that where you omit the dash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 353.64,
          "end": 355.68,
          "en": "and the character after the dash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.68,
          "end": 358.83,
          "en": "simply is that capital character now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 363.15,
          "en": "And then you could set this to red here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 363.15,
          "end": 365.76,
          "en": "or to make it really dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 365.76,
          "end": 370.18,
          "en": "check if box A is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.18,
          "end": 375.18,
          "en": "So if this data property here is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 375.88,
          "end": 379.57,
          "en": "and use a ternary expression to check if that is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 379.57,
          "end": 380.62,
          "en": "So if it's true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 380.62,
          "end": 383.6,
          "en": "and if that's the case after the question mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.6,
          "end": 385.323,
          "en": "we set this to red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 386.25,
          "end": 390.33,
          "en": "Otherwise we set it to this gray color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 390.33,
          "end": 391.743,
          "en": "So to this hex code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 392.65999999999997,
          "end": 396.12,
          "en": "And that's a default ternary expression in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 396.12,
          "end": 399.6,
          "en": "which we can use here since we're binding this dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 399.6,
          "end": 403.43,
          "en": "This object syntax is a special feature supported by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 403.43,
          "end": 406.98,
          "en": "for the style attributes specifically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 406.98,
          "end": 408.87,
          "en": "If I now saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 408.87,
          "end": 412.71,
          "en": "we initially have this gray border color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 412.71,
          "end": 416.78,
          "en": "but if I click on this box, it gets red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 416.78,
          "end": 419.64,
          "en": "Now there's no way of turning it back to gray at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.64,
          "end": 423.06,
          "en": "because we have no way of making it unselected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 423.06,
          "end": 424.74,
          "en": "but that's not a problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 424.74,
          "end": 427.95,
          "en": "because I want to focus on the dynamic styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.95,
          "end": 431.64,
          "en": "And that is how you could set up styles dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 431.64,
